+# BLUE CURRENT V51.40.0 — LIVE FLOOR & SERVICE CERTIFICATION
+
+V51.36–V51.40 certifies Blue Current's live dining-room and service continuity using the existing floor, reservation, waitlist, staffing, service-flow, and event models.
+
+## Ordered floor/service certification
+
+1. TABLE_STATE
+2. OCCUPANCY
+3. SECTION_SERVER_ASSIGNMENT
+4. RESERVATION_TABLE_LINKAGE
+5. WAITLIST_TABLE_LINKAGE
+6. TABLE_TURNS_RESET
+7. SERVICE_TIMING
+8. GUEST_MOVEMENT
+9. SEATING_PRESSURE
+10. SERVICE_EVENT_CONTINUITY
+
+The sequence is enforced.
+
+## System evidence versus human proof
+
+Each stage separates:
+
+- existing system evidence
+- human rehearsal/checkpoint evidence
+- final human certification
+
+A system-evidence gap does not become a pass.
+
+A controlled rehearsal may continue through a known evidence gap only with a documented override reason.
+
+## Existing operating systems are reused
+
+V51.40 reads from the existing:
+
+- FloorService
+- reservation/table links
+- waitlist/table links
+- sections
+- staff/server assignments
+- ServiceCoordinationService
+- seating events
+- live service events
+
+Certification itself does not mutate table state or move guests.
+
+## Occupancy model
+
+Occupancy is derived from authoritative table state:
+
+- current table status
+- party size
+- configured seat count
+
+The certification surface displays:
+
+- tables
+- sections
+- occupied tables
+- occupied seats
+- seat capacity
+- occupancy %
+- reservation/table linkage
+- waitlist count
+- service-flow count
+- service-event count
+
+## Current authenticated Chefs runtime
+
+Current state:
+
+`live-floor-service-ready`
+
+Across five in-scope restaurants:
+
+- 50 total floor/service stages
+- 7 have supporting system evidence
+- 0 have human checkpoint evidence
+- 0 are certified
+
+Marina Grille:
+
+- system evidence: 7/10
+- current derived occupancy: 18%
+- current evidence gaps:
+  - WAITLIST_TABLE_LINKAGE
+  - GUEST_MOVEMENT
+  - SERVICE_EVENT_CONTINUITY
+
+Harbor House, River & Rail, The Cabin, and Garden Social currently have 0/10 supporting floor/service stages because their authoritative live operating data has not yet been populated.
+
+## Validation edge case caught before release
+
+The first synthetic regression fixture produced 9/10 instead of 10/10.
+
+The certification service was correct: the fixture had historical seated-waitlist evidence, but no guest still waiting and only 50% occupancy, so there was no actual seating-pressure evidence.
+
+The fixture was corrected to include both:
+
+- seated waitlist-to-table continuity
+- an active waiting guest
+
+The complete clean regression was then rerun successfully.
+
+## Safety policy
+
+- existing floor/service workflow reused
+- table state read-only for certification
+- occupancy derived from authoritative state
+- human checkpoint evidence required
+- evidence-gap override requires reason
+- stage order enforced
+- certification human required
+- no synthetic floor pass
+- no automatic table mutation
+- no automatic guest movement
+- autonomous production changes false
+
+## Validation
+
+- V51.40 focused floor/service lifecycle PASS
+- all 10 ordered floor/service stages exercised PASS
+- table-state continuity PASS
+- occupancy accuracy PASS
+- section/server assignment PASS
+- reservation-table linkage PASS
+- waitlist-table linkage PASS
+- table turns/reset PASS
+- service timing PASS
+- guest movement PASS
+- seating pressure PASS
+- service-event continuity PASS
+- stage-order guard PASS
+- evidence-gap override guard PASS
+- V51.35 regression PASS
+- authenticated floor/service endpoint PASS
+- authoritative database unchanged
+- undefined module exports: 0
+- duplicate HTML IDs: 0
+- npm run check PASS
+- 941 JavaScript files
+- 786 client scripts
+- 5,870 unique HTML IDs
+
+## Next
+
+V51.41–V51.45 — Management & Executive Accuracy
+
+- operational KPI source tracing
+- dashboard-to-source reconciliation
+- occupancy / covers / wait accuracy
+- labor / service / kitchen signal integrity
+- profitability signal provenance
+- portfolio/location rollup accuracy
+- stale-data detection
+- metric discrepancy reporting
